<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>A death toll of four hundred — doubling overnight — is the measure of Pakistan's cross-border strikes on Kabul, which Taliban authorities say destroyed a functioning hospital while the world's attention remained fixed on the Iran war.</s>
<s>Pakistan insists every target was a military installation; Taliban leaders have promised a measured response and called for the Red Cross and the World Health Organization to be granted access to verify.</s>
<s>Neither organization has been allowed in.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran's navy vowed deadly retaliation after a United States submarine sank the warship <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="aɪrɪs ˈdɛnə">IRIS Dena</phoneme> on the fourth of March, killing eighty-seven sailors — the first Iranian vessel lost in combat since the Iran-Iraq war.</s>
<s>That same day, drones struck <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fuːˈdʒaɪrə">Fujairah</phoneme>'s oil storage hub east of the Strait of Hormuz for the second time in forty-eight hours, and no group claimed responsibility.</s>
<s>Tehran's drone-and-mine arsenal makes Gulf energy infrastructure the most likely target for any counterstrike.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Twenty-five days into American strikes on Iran, House Minority Leader <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="həˈkiːm ˈdʒɛfriz">Hakeem Jeffries</phoneme> became the first senior member of Congress to call the campaign a reckless war of choice — launched without an authorization vote.</s>
<s>No Democrat has filed a war powers resolution, leaving the administration's authority legally unchallenged.</s>
<s>A national survey this week placed public support for Israel at thirty-two percent — a historic low.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba's national grid collapsed under a United States oil blockade in January, plunging nine point six million people into blackouts lasting up to twenty hours a day.</s>
<s>Havana's response was to offer exile Cubans the right to own businesses for the first time since nineteen sixty-one — the most significant economic opening since the Revolution — while early diplomatic contacts with Washington began.</s>
<s>President Trump's public answer was not negotiation: he said the United States would take Cuba.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sri Lanka has cancelled Wednesdays — declaring them a mandatory rest day across government and schools not for any occasion, but to conserve oil.</s>
<s>The country imports nearly all its crude through the Strait of Hormuz, now blocked for three weeks, and private cars are rationed to fifteen litres per fill.</s>
<s>Drivers say fifteen litres is not enough to reach work.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Four billion dollars in South African fruit passes through shipping routes now blocked by fighting near the Strait of Hormuz and the Red Sea — and this season's harvest has nowhere to go.</s>
<s>Citrus and grapes are perishable, with no strategic reserve, so every shipping day lost is produce that spoils.</s>
<s>Farmers in South Africa are paying the price of a Gulf war they had no part in starting.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Japan raised permanent residency fees by two thousand nine hundred percent, effective immediately for existing residents renewing their status.</s>
<s>The ruling coalition passed the measure despite record vacancies in Japan's service sector, with conservative lawmakers arguing that artificial intelligence and automation will fill the gap.</s>
<s>Population has declined for fifteen consecutive years.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's president proposed restricting civilian driving as the Strait of Hormuz enters its third week of closure.</s>
<s>President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="liː dʒeɪ mjʌŋ">Lee Jae Myung</phoneme> cited the country's seventy percent dependence on Hormuz crude while declining to send warships to reopen the strait, citing constitutional limits on military deployment.</s>
<s>Seoul would join Sri Lanka as the only nations to mandate civilian sacrifice for a conflict they did not start.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Malaysia last week retracted a declaration tied to its two hundred and forty billion dollar trade deal with the United States, after Washington launched investigations into nearly sixty partner nations.</s>
<s>The five-month negotiation window set when the deal was signed in October expires this month, leaving Malaysia waiting for new American terms.</s>
<s>It is a pattern now visible across dozens of countries: sign with goodwill, then negotiate under pressure.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A joint Chinese and Chilean research vessel reached the floor of the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌætəˈkɑːmə">Atacama</phoneme> Trench — one of the Pacific's deepest points — in an expedition Chile's navy approved despite sustained American diplomatic pressure.</s>
<s>Washington had revoked the visas of Chilean diplomats in protest of China-funded scientific projects, warning that cooperation could serve military ends.</s>
<s>Chile has not broken with Beijing, and the vessel departed from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌvælpəˈreɪsoʊ">Valparaíso</phoneme> as planned.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Oxford undergraduate has advanced a sixty-year mathematics problem that predicts each runner moving at a unique speed around a circular track will eventually stand alone.</s>
<s>The Lonely Runner Conjecture connects number theory, geometry, and graph theory, and has resisted formal proof since the nineteen-sixties.</s>
<s>Research now covers ten runners, up from seven in two thousand and seven; eleven remains the unsolved frontier.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Mistral, the French artificial intelligence company, released <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="liːnstrəl">Leanstral</phoneme> — an open-source agent that writes code and then proves, mathematically, that the code is correct.</s>
<s>The system uses Lean four, a formal proof assistant, to verify software against mathematical specifications rather than relying on test coverage, which can miss edge cases.</s>
<s>Model weights and a new benchmark for formal proof were published under an open license.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>